[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Software requirements
UID: DOC-SWR
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Conventions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Each requirement names the module that implements it. Code and tests point back
at a requirement with a marker inside their Doxygen comment, in the form
``@relation(SWR-PI-001, scope=function)``. ``make docs`` fails when a marker
names a UID that this document does not define. ``make trace`` fails when a
requirement has no test.

Units: speed in rpm (``rpm_t``), current in mA (``milliamp_t``), and duty in
permille from -1000 to 1000 (``duty_permille_t``). The sign of the duty sets
the direction of rotation.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Domain: PI controller

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-PI-001
TITLE: Proportional-integral output
STATEMENT: >>>
``pi_step`` shall return ``Kp * e + I``, clamped to ``[out_min, out_max]``,
where ``e`` is the speed error and ``I`` is the accumulated integral term
``sum(Ki * e)``. Gains are Q8 fixed-point integers, so a gain of 256 is 1.0.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-PI-002
TITLE: Integrator anti-windup
STATEMENT: >>>
The integral term shall stay within the output limits, and shall not grow
further while the output is saturated in the direction of the error.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Without this, a long saturation stores a large integral that overshoots the
setpoint when the load releases.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-PI-003
TITLE: Controller reset
STATEMENT: >>>
``pi_reset`` shall set the integral term to zero.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Domain: motor state machine

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-FSM-001
TITLE: Motor states
STATEMENT: >>>
The motor state machine shall have the states ``IDLE``, ``RUNNING`` and
``FAULT``, and shall start in ``IDLE``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-FSM-002
TITLE: Start and stop transitions
STATEMENT: >>>
The ``START`` event shall move ``IDLE`` to ``RUNNING``. The ``STOP`` event
shall move ``RUNNING`` to ``IDLE``. Any other event in those states shall leave
the state unchanged, except ``FAULT``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-FSM-003
TITLE: Fault entry and acknowledge
STATEMENT: >>>
The ``FAULT`` event shall move every state to ``FAULT``. In ``FAULT``, only
``CLEAR_FAULT`` shall change the state, and it shall move to ``IDLE``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Domain: fault monitor

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-FLT-001
TITLE: Overcurrent detection
STATEMENT: >>>
``fault_monitor_step`` shall report ``FAULT_OVERCURRENT`` in the same call in
which the absolute motor current exceeds ``overcurrent_ma``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-FLT-002
TITLE: Stall detection
STATEMENT: >>>
``fault_monitor_step`` shall report ``FAULT_STALL`` when, for ``stall_ticks``
consecutive calls, the absolute duty is at least ``stall_min_duty`` and the
absolute speed is below ``stall_max_speed_rpm``. A call that breaks either
condition shall restart the count.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Domain: motor control

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-CTL-001
TITLE: Setpoint clamp and ramp
STATEMENT: >>>
``motor_control_set_speed`` shall clamp the target to
``[-max_setpoint_rpm, max_setpoint_rpm]``. Each ``motor_control_step`` call
shall move the ramped setpoint toward the target by at most
``ramp_rpm_per_tick``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-CTL-002
TITLE: Drive disabled outside RUNNING
STATEMENT: >>>
In every state other than ``RUNNING``, ``motor_control_step`` shall return a
drive command with ``enable = false`` and ``duty = 0``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-CTL-003
TITLE: Bumpless start
STATEMENT: >>>
On entering ``RUNNING``, the controller shall reset the PI controller and start
the ramped setpoint at the measured speed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Starting the ramp at the measured speed avoids a step in duty when the operator
restarts a motor that is still coasting.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-CTL-004
TITLE: Same-step fault shutdown
STATEMENT: >>>
When the fault monitor reports a fault, ``motor_control_step`` shall latch the
fault flags, move the state machine to ``FAULT``, and return a disabled drive
command in that same call. ``CLEAR_FAULT`` shall clear the latched flags.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Middleware: scheduler

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-SCH-001
TITLE: Fixed-period cooperative scheduling
STATEMENT: >>>
``sched_run`` shall call each task whose period has elapsed since its last run,
in table order, once per call. It shall keep the period correct when the
millisecond tick wraps around ``UINT32_MAX``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Board support package

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-BSP-001
TITLE: Encoder speed conversion
STATEMENT: >>>
``bsp_motor_sample`` shall compute the speed from the change of the 16-bit
encoder count since the previous sample, the board's counts per revolution and
the 1 ms sample period. The result shall be correct when the counter wraps.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-BSP-002
TITLE: Current conversion
STATEMENT: >>>
``bsp_motor_sample`` shall convert the raw ADC reading of the current-sense
channel to mA with the board's scale and offset.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-BSP-003
TITLE: Drive command mapping
STATEMENT: >>>
``bsp_motor_apply`` shall set the direction pin from the sign of the duty, set
the PWM duty to the absolute duty, and set the bridge enable pin from
``enable``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-BSP-004
TITLE: Checked initialisation
STATEMENT: >>>
``bsp_init`` shall check the status of every HAL initialisation call and return
``false`` if any call fails.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-006

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Application

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-APP-001
TITLE: Task periods
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall run the control task every 1 ms and the user interface
task every 10 ms.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-APP-002
TITLE: Button events
STATEMENT: >>>
A rising edge of the start button shall send ``START``. A rising edge of the
stop button shall send ``CLEAR_FAULT`` in ``FAULT`` and ``STOP`` in every other
state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Architecture constraints

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-ARC-001
TITLE: Layer include rule
STATEMENT: >>>
Source files shall include only headers from the layers they may depend on:
``app`` on ``app``, ``domain``, ``middleware`` and ``bsp``. ``domain`` on
``domain``. ``middleware`` on ``middleware``. ``bsp`` on ``bsp``, ``hal`` and
``domain``. ``hal`` on ``hal``. Only ``src/hal/port`` may include vendor
headers. ``tools/check_layers.py`` enforces this rule.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-006
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SWR-DET-001
TITLE: No heap and no floating point
STATEMENT: >>>
Source files outside ``src/hal/port`` shall not call ``malloc``, ``calloc``,
``realloc`` or ``free``, and shall not use ``float`` or ``double``.
``tools/check_layers.py`` enforces this rule.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-007

[[/SECTION]]
